<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were steady to softer on Wednesday as banks stayed liquid following the remittance of billions of pesos of income tax payments early this week, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market didn't tighten,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said.</p>
<p>The one, two and 12-month rates were lower, while the rest were steady.</p>
<p>The dealer said the huge amount of tenders worth 12.87 billion pesos for the maiden issue of 20-year treasury bonds on Tuesday was a reflection of the very liquid market.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  APRIL 23		 APRIL 22</p>
<p>    1 W		9 11/16		 9 11/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9 11/16		 9 11/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9  3/4		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    2 M		9 13/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    3 M		9 15/16		 9 15/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  3/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  3/8		 10  7/16</p>
<p>    VAL		24-Apr		  23-Apr</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 84108937</p>
